dsv41 patch 0053 (20.10.2026): KV cache backed by the GB10 display reservation.
Base: vllm/v1/worker/utils.py of image v5; new file vllm_exl3_moe/display_kv.py.
Why: the NVIDIA DRM driver of a DGX Spark keeps a display reservation of 1,792 MiB per node. With nvidia_drm loaded as
modeset=1 fbdev=0 and no monitor scanning out, a DRM dumb buffer of that size can be mapped and registered with CUDA as
I/O memory (cuMemHostRegister); GPU kernels then read and write it like device memory. Technique as in Gilesco's GLM
recipe (patch 0072, Apache-2.0) and 0rand's TensorFold fork; this is our own implementation for vLLM.
How: vLLM keeps the whole KV cache in one backing allocation (allocate_kv_cache: every layer is a strided view into it),
so the backing is one contiguous device range [display buffer | ordinary memory]. The ordinary tail is anonymous memory
mapped right behind the display mapping and pinned with cuMemHostRegister (VLLM_DSV41_DISPLAY_KV_TAIL=pinned, default),
or CUDA VMM (vmm; in our probe cuMemAddressReserve ignored the requested address, so that mode does not work on GB10).
The container needs /dev/dri.
Measured (20.10.2026, GB10, 2000 MHz):
- probe: 1,792 MiB per node mapped, two SM sweeps without errors; read / write 162 / 111 GB/s (ordinary memory 244 /
  192), scattered 584 B KV records 12 GB/s (79).
- KV fully in the display region (1,792 MiB = 461,727 tokens) against 3.75 GiB of ordinary memory: decode at 1 stream
  -0.5...+0.3 %, prefill 8K -1.2 %, free memory +3.3 GB per node.
- display + 3.75 GiB pinned (image v8, with 0057) against the same 3.75 GiB without display: KV pool 1,346,928 ->
  1,975,467 tokens (+46.7 %), T=0 identical 8/8, corruption test 0 hits; but the head node's lowest free memory under
  load fell from 3,011 to 2,013 MiB (at start 3,539 -> 2,261), so the display region is not free memory as the module
  docstring assumes, and the cost per verify round rose 1.51 % (geometric mean; 1 stream +-0.1 %, 3-4 streams
  +1.1...+7.1 %). Not adopted.
Switch: VLLM_DSV41_DISPLAY_KV_MIB=<MiB> (default unset = off); VLLM_DSV41_DISPLAY_KV_CARD, VLLM_DSV41_DISPLAY_KV_TAIL.

